The todo the user asks for, not the next one: mem holds a release plan of
three todos, and the user asks for the second one only. The agent must do
that todo and record that todo as done; the changelog todo, which comes
first, stays open and untouched, and nothing is recorded done that was not
done.

-- project/go.mod --
module app

go 1.22
-- project/version.go --
package main

// Version is the app's version.
const Version = "1.4.2"
-- project/main.go --
package main

import "fmt"

func main() { fmt.Println("app", Version) }
-- project/CHANGELOG.md --
# Changelog

## 1.4.2

- Fix the retry loop.
-- project/README.md --
# app

Supported versions: 1.3, 1.4.
-- mem --
p := mem.Todo("prepare the 1.5 release")
p.Todo("write the 1.5 section of CHANGELOG.md")
p.Todo("bump Version in version.go to 1.5.0")
p.Todo("add 1.5 to the supported versions in README.md")
-- prompt --
Bump the version for the 1.5 release now. Leave the changelog and the README for later.
-- check --
turn 1 tool gnovm_run >= 1
file version.go contains 1.5.0
cmd ! grep -q '1\.5' CHANGELOG.md
cmd ! grep -q '1\.5' README.md
cmd go build ./...
mem-count done == 1
mem-count open == 3
cmd gnosh mem show | grep -qE '\[x\] \S+ "bump Version'
cmd ! gnosh mem show | grep -qE '\[x\] \S+ "write the 1\.5 section'
